Keep MP3 gapless metadata when the stream size is unknown.

avio_size() is negative for an HTTP response without Content-Length. Stored
in a uint64_t it became a huge file size, so the Xing/LAME frame count was
discarded as an "invalid concatenated file" and the encoder padding at the
end of each track was played.

--- a/libavformat/mp3dec.c
+++ b/libavformat/mp3dec.c
@@ -173,9 +173,11 @@
 
     MP3DecContext *mp3 = s->priv_data;
     static const int64_t xing_offtbl[2][2] = {{32, 17}, {17,9}};
-    uint64_t fsize = avio_size(s->pb);
+    int64_t size = avio_size(s->pb);
     int64_t pos = avio_tell(s->pb);
-    fsize = fsize >= pos ? fsize - pos : 0;
+    /* An unknown size (for example an HTTP stream without Content-Length) is
+     * negative; it must not be compared as a huge unsigned file size. */
+    uint64_t fsize = size >= pos ? size - pos : 0;
 
     /* Check for Xing / Info tag */
     avio_skip(s->pb, xing_offtbl[c->lsf == 1][c->nb_channels == 1]);
